Hydrocarbons: Alkanes (CnH2n+2) are saturated; alkenes (CnH2n) have C=C; alkynes (CnH2n-2) have C≡C; aromatic compounds based on benzene ring.

Periodic table: Elements arranged by atomic number; periodic trends in radius, ionization energy, electronegativity; s, p, d, f blocks based on orbital type.

Applied chemistry: Petrochemical industry, polymer science, green chemistry principles; importance of sustainable chemical manufacturing for environmental protection.</td></tr></table><!-- academic-extension:start --><section class="academic-extension" aria-labelledby="academic-extension-title"><h2 id="academic-extension-title">Academic Extension: Evidence, Conditions &amp; Open Questions</h2><p><b>Topic bridge — Foundation And Fundamentals.</b> Use this extension to connect the topic’s core material with deeper academic inquiry: state a claim, name the conditions under which it holds, and distinguish established knowledge from an open research or interpretive question.</p><h3>Established academic fact</h3><p>Chemical properties arise from the arrangement and interaction of electrons and nuclei. Conservation of atoms and charge constrains reactions; molecular structure and energy changes help explain which products form.</p><h3>Conditions, assumptions &amp; limits</h3><p>Treat oxidation state, bonding diagrams and reaction equations as models with defined rules. Temperature, pressure, solvent, concentration, particle size and catalysts can alter rates or equilibria; name the conditions whenever comparing results.</p><h3>Open research question — How chemistry led to the first living systems</h3><p>Life’s existence and subsequent evolution are established, but the detailed sequence by which non-living chemistry produced self-sustaining living systems remains unresolved. Researchers investigate plausible molecules and environments without treating any single pathway as proven.</p><h3>Inquiry prompt</h3><p>For “Foundation And Fundamentals”, identify one assumption in the model, explain what observation would test it, and state what evidence could distinguish the accepted account from the open question “How chemistry led to the first living systems”.</p><h3>Further reading</h3><ul><li><a href="https://openstax.org/books/chemistry-2e/pages/13-1-chemical-equilibria">OpenStax Chemistry: chemical equilibrium</a></li><li><a href="https://openstax.org/books/chemistry-2e/pages/6-5-periodic-variations-in-element-properties">OpenStax Chemistry: periodic trends</a></li><li><a href="https://astrobiology.nasa.gov/research/">NASA Astrobiology: research questions</a></li></ul><p><small>Curriculum note: the research question is an enrichment extension, not a claim that the established school-level model is invalid. Check the prescribed NEB text and syllabus for examinable scope.</small></p></section><!-- academic-extension:end --></body></html>